From b9899fa81aa55730a720755569023ba1d94677bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chaton <definitelyfrenchname@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 12:34:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?cps2w:=20the=20CPS-2=20Turbo=20object=20promote?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20=E2=80=94=20a=203-bit=20GFX=20bank=20(slice=20D3)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Stock CPS-2 reads an object's graphics bank from two bits of the frame
table's y-word (`st3_bank <= table_y[14:13]`), so a 16-bit tile code plus a
2-bit bank is an 18-bit tile address: 32 MB of graphics, and that is the cap.
CPS-2 WIDE needs 48 MB, i.e. a third bank bit.

The free bit is y bit 12, and it can only be read AFTER the sprite-list
terminator test, which is the whole of the rule. y bit 15 IS the terminator:
setting it on a live sprite ends the list and drops every later sprite. Capcom
solved the same problem the same way on CPS-2 Turbo — test bit 15 first, then
promote bit 12 into it, then read a 3-bit bank from bits 15:13. Inside the
else arm of the terminator test bit 15 is known to be zero, so the promoted
bank is exactly { y[12], y[14:13] }.

  cores/cps2w/hdl/jtcps2_obj_scan.v  the promote, ANDed with wide_en
  cores/cps2w/hdl/jtcps2_obj.v       the 3-bit bank wire and output
  cores/cps2w/hdl/jtcps1_obj_draw.v  3-bit bank in and out; width only
  cores/cps2w/hdl/jtcps1_video.v     3-bit rom0_bank out, wide_en in
  cores/cps2w/hdl/jtcps2_game.v      rom0_bank[2] untied; wide_en to video

Bit 2 reaches jtcps1_sdram's `gfxc_sel`, which the previous commit placed and
gated but left unreachable because the game top tied that bit low. It is now
driven, so the two group-C read slots — the tenant graphics in SDRAM banks 1
and 0 — are reachable for the first time.

Gated twice over: the promote itself is ANDed with wide_en (the runtime MRA
header bit), so with the profile clear bit 2 is zero at its source, and
gfxc_sel is ANDed with wide_en at its destination. The reference cores
cores/cps1, cores/cps2 and cores/cps15 stay byte-untouched; every file that
had to differ is a copy under cores/cps2w/hdl and the diff against the
original is the whole of the change.
---
 cores/cps2w/cfg/game.yaml          |  19 +-
 cores/cps2w/hdl/jtcps1_obj_draw.v  | 165 +++++++
 cores/cps2w/hdl/jtcps1_video.v     | 694 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 cores/cps2w/hdl/jtcps2_game.v      |  31 +-
 cores/cps2w/hdl/jtcps2_obj.v       | 224 ++++++++++
 cores/cps2w/hdl/jtcps2_obj_scan.v  | 243 ++++++++++
 cores/cps2w/hdl/jtcps2w_obj_bank.v |  66 +++
 7 files changed, 1428 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 cores/cps2w/hdl/jtcps1_obj_draw.v
 create mode 100644 cores/cps2w/hdl/jtcps1_video.v
 create mode 100644 cores/cps2w/hdl/jtcps2_obj.v
